# Tracer: builtin integer divisibility predicate
#
# Before (did not work):
# $dvd(12, 3)
# Former behavior: WellDefinedError: fact `dvd` not defined.
#
# Now (verified):
$dvd(12, 3)
# Current behavior: the nonzero integer 3 divides the integer 12.

forall x Z, y Z*:
    x % y = 0
    =>:
        $dvd(x, y)

forall x Z, y Z*:
    $dvd(x, y)
    =>:
        x % y = 0
        exist a Z st {x = a * y}

# Boundary: `$dvd(7, 3)` and every zero-divisor application remain rejected;
# the executable negative regressions live in `native_number_theory.rs`.
# Evidence: target/release/litex -compact -isolated -runner -f examples/02_builtin_math/dvd.lit
